<title>USA: U.S. 2-year note auction high yield 5.984 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. 2-year note auction high yield 5.984 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Treasury said its Dutch bidding auction of 2-year notes produced these results:</p>
<p>			 2-YEAR NOTES DUE JAN 31, 1999</p>
<p>			     $17.503 BILLION AUCTION</p>
<p>	     YIELD			  PRICE	COUPON</p>
<p> HIGH	5.984    Awarded At	99.797	5.875</p>
<p> MEDIAN    5.970    High Yield	NOT GIVEN  Percent</p>
<p> LOW	 5.931    16 Percent	NOT GIVEN</p>
<p>	   Cover - (Bids Over Amount Sold)    =  2.44 Times</p>
<p> U.S. TREASURY (GOVERNMENT DEBT)		 MATURITY 31.Jan.99</p>
<p> MATURITY/TYPE    2-YEAR NOTES		   PAY DATE 31.Jan.97</p>
<p> TYPE OF DEBT     STRAIGHT			 LAUNCHED 22.Jan.97</p>
<p> ISSUED/ACCEPTED  17.503 BLN USD		 CUSIP    9128272F8</p>
<p> BIDS SUBMITTED   42.692			   COUNTRY	  USA</p>
<p> NONCOMPETITIVE    1.651				DUTCH AUCTION</p>
